        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: avoid native i18n branch regex backtracking",
        "body": "Related: CodeQL alert #557\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where PR-controlled native app source text could make the native i18n inventory check spend excessive CPU time when a conditional branch string hit a backtracking-heavy identifier regex.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe conditional-branch identifier check now uses a small linear ASCII scanner instead of a nested-quantifier regular expression. This preserves the existing camelCase-style filtering behavior while removing the CodeQL `js/redos` path from the CI native i18n lane.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers and contributors get a more resilient native i18n CI check. There is no product UI behavior change.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, implemented with Codex.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm format:fix -- scripts/native-app-i18n.ts test/scripts/native-app-i18n.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/native-app-i18n.test.ts`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local`\n- Autoreview result: `autoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported`\n- `git diff --check`\n",
